# menu-app is the source of truth

This prototype re-creates Management Center (MC) menu building with better UX. It lives next to `../menu-app`, which defines what is real.

## Before adding or changing a setting

- Find how MC does it in `../menu-app/frontend-migration/libs/management-center-app/feature-menu-products` and the components in `../menu-app/frontend-migration/libs/admin-ui`.
- Check backend entities in `../menu-app/backend/libs/core/src/Entities` for field names, enums and numeric state values. Never guess them.
- If the prototype has something MC or the backend doesn't support, flag it and ask whether to keep it.

## Copy

- Follow `../menu-app/docs/design/ux-copy-principles.md` for every label, help text, error and dialog.
- When existing prototype copy or MC copy conflicts with the principles, ask before changing it. State the conflict, the principle, and the proposed wording.

## This repo is public

- Re-create behaviour and wording; never copy MC source files, internal docs, credentials, or real customer and store data into this repo.

## Prototype conventions

- Plain JS, no build step: `index.html`, `styles.css`, `data.js` and `data-cravewave.js` (seed data), and classic scripts in `js/` that share one global scope and load in the order listed in `index.html`:
  - `core.js`: constants, formatting and validation utils, icons.
  - `state.js`: `S`, `T`, `ctx`, entity defaults and migrations, POS lookups and price caches, stores, seed, persistence, undo.
  - `model.js`: paths and entity lookups, group rules, half-and-half matching, prices, size sets.
  - `derived.js`: `derivedCtx`, `computeIssues`, compare data, input binding.
  - `mutations.js`: selection, add pickers, link, unlink and remove.
  - `drop-sync.js`: drop resolution, auto-place, POS load and sync, publish, export.
  - `compare-optimize.js`: Compare to POS, Optimize and half-and-half dialogs.
  - `render.js`: `render`, topbar, POS panel, canvas tree rows.
  - `inspector.js`: form control helpers, `renderInspector`.
  - `inspector-menu.js`, `inspector-product.js`, `inspector-group.js`: inspector tabs per kind (menu file also has the category tab).
  - `preview.js`: customer preview.
  - `overlays.js`: popovers, modals, pickers, toasts, row and app menus, image reading.
  - `actions.js`: `handleAction`.
  - `events.js`: DOM listeners, drag and drop, keyboard.
  - `main.js`: boot; must stay last.
- Top-level code that runs on load may only use names from the same or earlier files; functions called from handlers can live anywhere.
- Reuse existing CSS tokens and helpers in `js/` before adding new ones.
- No comments that narrate the code.
- Verify in the browser: `python3 -m http.server 5178 --bind 127.0.0.1`, then open `http://127.0.0.1:5178/`.
- Pushing to `main` publishes to https://ddrlacic.github.io/menu-builder-prototype/ within about a minute.
